  "claim": "Of the PSI tests that reached 30% oxygen or more, 8 of 32 droplet tests and 66 of 468 gas tests also ran at or below 10.2 psi; for solids and smoke there is no data, because some of their tests report no oxygen.",
  "summary_student": "NASA tested many droplet and gas flames at 30% oxygen or more, the oxygen level planned for a lunar habitat, but only some of those tests were also run at the habitat's lower pressure of 10.2 psi or less: 8 droplet tests and 66 gas tests. For solid materials and smoke, the tables do not report the oxygen level of every test, so this count gives no answer for them; that is not the same as zero, and it says nothing about whether solids are safe or unsafe.",
  "summary_professional": "Applying the lunar_base atmosphere (O2 at least 30%, pressure at most 10.2 psi) to the PSI tests table: droplet phase, 32 tests reached the O2 threshold, of which 8 also met the pressure limit and 0 report no pressure (PSI-68 FLEX-2, PSI-69 FLEX). Gas phase, 468 tests reached the O2 threshold, of which 66 also met the pressure limit and 36 report no pressure (PSI-10 Flame Design, PSI-159 CFI-G, PSI-20 ACME BRE). Total n = 500 tests at or above the O2 threshold. Solid and smoke phases are omitted from the values because some of their tests report no O2: the result for them is no data, not zero.",
